# Query LLM Frontend - Claude Rules

## Project Context
This is a Next.js 16 React application with TypeScript, using App Router, TanStack Query, Firebase Auth, and Tailwind CSS.

## Cross-Repo Links
- Root index: `AGENTS.md`

## Critical Conventions

### Naming Rules
- **Components**: PascalCase - `LoginForm`, `ChatInput`, `Sidebar`
- **Pages**: lowercase - `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`
- **Hooks**: kebab-case + `use-` - `use-auth.ts`, `use-conversation-queries.ts`
- **Variables**: camelCase - `userData`, `isLoading`, `conversationId`
- **Functions**: camelCase - `handleSubmit()`, `fetchData()`, `validateInput()`
- **Types**: PascalCase + `T` prefix - `TUser`, `TConversation`, `TApiResponse`
- **Constants**: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE - `API_BASE_URL`, `MAX_RETRIES`

### Architecture Layers

| Layer | Purpose | Location |
|-------|---------|----------|
| Pages | Route handlers | `src/app/` |
| Components | Reusable UI | `src/components/` |
| Hooks (API) | Backend integration | `src/hooks/api/` |
| Hooks (Custom) | Local state/logic | `src/hooks/custom/` |
| Providers | Context/global state | `src/components/providers/` |
| Types | TypeScript definitions | `src/types/` |
| Lib | Utilities/config | `src/lib/` |

## Standard Patterns

### New API Hook Template
```typescript
import { useMutation, useQuery } from "@tanstack/react-query";
import { api } from "@/lib/api";
import { queryClient } from "@/lib/tanstack-query";
import type { TEntity } from "@/types";
import type { TApiPromise, TMutationOpts, TQueryOpts } from "@/types/tanstack-query";

export type TGetEntityArgs = { entityId: string };
export type TGetEntityResult = TEntity;

export const useGetEntity = (
  args: TGetEntityArgs,
  options?: TQueryOpts<TGetEntityResult>
) => {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ["useGetEntity", args],
    queryFn: () => api.get(`/entities/${args.entityId}`) as TApiPromise<TGetEntityResult>,
    enabled: !!args.entityId,
    ...options,
  });
};

export type TCreateEntityArgs = { name: string };
export type TCreateEntityResult = void;

export const useCreateEntity = (
  options?: TMutationOpts<TCreateEntityArgs, TCreateEntityResult>
) => {
  return useMutation({
    mutationKey: ["useCreateEntity"],
    mutationFn: (args) => api.post("/entities/", args) as TApiPromise<TCreateEntityResult>,
    ...options,
    onSuccess: (...data) => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["useGetEntity"] });
      options?.onSuccess?.(...data);
    },
  });
};
```

### New Page Template
```typescript
"use client";

import { useAuth } from "@/hooks/custom/use-auth";
import { useRouter } from "next/navigation";
import { useEffect } from "react";

export default function PageName() {
  const { user, loading } = useAuth();
  const router = useRouter();

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!loading && !user) {
      router.push("/login");
    }
  }, [user, loading, router]);

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (!user) return null;

  return <div>Content</div>;
}
```

### New Component Template
```typescript
"use client";

import { useState } from "react";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  onAction?: () => void;
}

export function Component({ title, onAction }: ComponentProps) {
  const [isActive, setIsActive] = useState(false);

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{title}</h2>
      <Button onClick={onAction}>Action</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Form Component Template
```typescript
"use client";

import { useForm } from "react-hook-form";
import { zodResolver } from "@hookform/resolvers/zod";
import { z } from "zod";
import { toast } from "sonner";
import {
  Form,
  FormControl,
  FormField,
  FormItem,
  FormLabel,
  FormMessage,
} from "@/components/ui/form";
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

const schema = z.object({
  field: z.string().min(1, "Required"),
});

type FormData = z.infer<typeof schema>;

export function MyForm() {
  const form = useForm<FormData>({
    resolver: zodResolver(schema),
    defaultValues: { field: "" },
  });

  const onSubmit = async (data: FormData) => {
    try {
      toast.success("Success!");
    } catch {
      toast.error("Error!");
    }
  };

  return (
    <Form {...form}>
      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
        <FormField
          control={form.control}
          name="field"
          render={({ field }) => (
            <FormItem>
              <FormLabel>Field</FormLabel>
              <FormControl>
                <Input {...field} />
              </FormControl>
              <FormMessage />
            </FormItem>
          )}
        />
        <Button type="submit" disabled={form.formState.isSubmitting}>
          Submit
        </Button>
      </form>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

## React Query Patterns

### Query Hook Checklist
- [ ] Export type for args: `TGetEntityArgs`
- [ ] Export type for result: `TGetEntityResult`
- [ ] Use descriptive queryKey: `["useGetEntity", args]`
- [ ] Cast return type: `as TApiPromise<TGetEntityResult>`
- [ ] Add `enabled` condition if needed
- [ ] Spread `options` parameter

### Mutation Hook Checklist
- [ ] Export type for args: `TCreateEntityArgs`
- [ ] Export type for result: `TCreateEntityResult`
- [ ] Use descriptive mutationKey: `["useCreateEntity"]`
- [ ] Cast return type: `as TApiPromise<TCreateEntityResult>`
- [ ] Invalidate related queries in `onSuccess`

## SOP Updates
- Do not use a separate `useGetMe` hook; use `useGetUser` with `GET /api/users/:user_id`.
- Message creation uses `PATCH /api/conversations/:conversation_id` with `message` payload.
- Create/Update/Delete endpoints return no `data` payloads in success responses.
- [ ] Call `options?.onSuccess?.(...data)`
- [ ] Spread `options` parameter

## Component Patterns

### Loading States
```typescript
if (isLoading) {
  return <div className="flex items-center justify-center p-8">
    <p className="text-muted-foreground">Loading...</p>
  </div>;
}
```

### Error States
```typescript
if (error) {
  return <div className="flex items-center justify-center p-8">
    <p className="text-destructive">Error: {error.message}</p>
  </div>;
}
```

### Empty States
```typescript
if (items.length === 0) {
  return <div className="flex flex-col items-center justify-center py-12">
    <Icon className="mb-4 size-12 text-muted-foreground" />
    <h2 className="mb-2 text-lg font-medium">No items</h2>
    <p className="text-muted-foreground">Get started by creating one</p>
    <Button onClick={handleCreate}>Create</Button>
  </div>;
}
```

## Authentication Flow

1. Firebase handles sign-in/sign-up
2. On sign-up, create user in backend via `useCreateUser`
3. Firebase token auto-attached to all API requests
4. Auth state managed by `AuthProvider`
5. Protected routes check `user` from `useAuth()`

```typescript
const { user, loading, signIn, signUp, signOut } = useAuth();
```

## Data Fetching Flow

1. Create types in `src/types/index.ts`
2. Create React Query hook in `src/hooks/api/{entity}.ts`
3. Use hook in component with loading/error handling
4. Mutations auto-invalidate related queries

```typescript
const { data, isLoading, error } = useGetConversations();
const mutation = useCreateConversation({
  onSuccess: () => toast.success("Created!"),
});
```

## Styling Approach

- Use Tailwind utility classes
- Use `cn()` for conditional classes
- Use shadcn/ui components
- Follow mobile-first responsive design
- Use design tokens (primary, muted, destructive, etc.)

```typescript
<div className={cn(
  "flex items-center gap-2 p-4",
  isActive && "bg-accent",
  !isActive && "opacity-50"
)} />
```

## Common Gotchas

1. **`"use client"` directive** - Required for interactive components
2. **`next/navigation` vs `next/router`** - Use `next/navigation`
3. **React Query invalidation** - Must happen in `onSuccess`
4. **Type prefixes** - Use `T` for all type names
5. **Path aliases** - Always use `@/` not `../`
6. **Loading states** - Always handle loading/error/empty
7. **Toast notifications** - Use for all mutations
8. **Form validation** - Always use Zod with React Hook Form

## Type Definitions

```typescript
export interface TEntity {
  id: string;
  field: string;
  created_at: Date;
  updated_at: Date;
}

export type TApiPromise<T> = Promise<AxiosResponse<TApiSuccessResponse<T>>>;

export type TQueryOpts<TData> = Omit<
  UseQueryOptions<AxiosResponse<TApiSuccessResponse<TData>>, Error, TData>,
  "queryKey" | "queryFn"
>;

export type TMutationOpts<TVariables, TData = void> = Omit<
  UseMutationOptions<AxiosResponse<TApiSuccessResponse<TData>>, Error, TVariables, unknown>,
  "mutationKey" | "mutationFn"
>;
```

